<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Backup rules (API < 31): Exclude encrypted prefs and legacy settings
    from Google cloud backup. Auth tokens and server credentials must not
    be backed up ... they could be restored to a different device.

    Entitlement prefs go in OPPOSITE directions, on purpose:
    - nine_lives_entitlement.xml (grandfather flag `legacy_paid`) MUST ride
      Auto Backup so a paid install survives reinstall and device transfer.
      It is deliberately NOT listed here: with no <include> rules, everything
      not excluded is backed up by default. Do NOT add an explicit <include>
      for it ... the first <include> flips this file to allowlist mode and
      silently drops every other pref from backup.
    - nine_lives_entitlement_cache.xml (cached Play grant + the release-build
      force-free test override) IS excluded below, and is excluded in both
      sections of data_extraction_rules.xml. A Play purchase belongs to a
      Google account, not a device; backing up the cache would turn it into a
      portable unlock for accounts that never paid, and the condition that
      would revoke it (a SUCCESSFUL empty query) can never fire on an account
      that never bought while Billing is unreachable.

    Note the asymmetry below: exclude is safe to add here, include is not.
    Adding the first <include> flips this whole file to allowlist mode and
    silently drops the grandfather flag along with everything else.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="nine_lives_secure_prefs.xml" />
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="nine_lives_entitlement_cache.xml" />
    <exclude domain="file" path="NineLivesAudio/settings.json" />
</full-backup-content>
